cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mixdyn"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ilia
    family-names: Gradina
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-0911-8765"
repository-code: "https://github.com/causaldyn/mixdyn"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/mixdyn/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-20"
abstract: >-
  A media-mix modelling (MMM) engine in Python and JAX: regressions, discount dynamic linear models,
  Bayesian models with lift and geo tests in the likelihood, geo hierarchies, test readers and budget
  plans, computed without a UI, built on causal-hybrid-control. Its one pre-registered run of the
  causaldyn bench is a non-inferiority result stated with its losses, not a claim to be best.
keywords:
  - marketing mix modeling
  - media mix modeling
  - causal inference
  - bayesian inference
  - budget allocation
  - lift tests
  - geo experiments
  - jax
